  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Beyond Compliance Consortium</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Beyond Compliance Consortium proposes a theoretical, empirical, and operational research programme designed to deliver on the vision articulated in the Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office (FCDO) Call &#x201c;Wars Fought Better: Building the evidence on promoting restraint by armed actors&#x201d;. The programme&#x2019;s aim is to contribute to the effective prevention and reduction of humanitarian needs and civilian harm, thus facilitating a broader protective environment in armed conflict. This objective will be achieved by improving the strategic understanding and operational and policy know-how of key stakeholders on what interventions are most effective in generating compliance and promoting restraint by a range of armed actors.</narrative>
  </description>
